NAME
    mount - mount a filesystem or bind a resource

SYNOPSIS
    mount
    mount -a
    mount <n> <path>
    mount -r <host:port> <path>
    mount -p | -c | -n <path>

DESCRIPTION
    With no argument, lists what is mounted. -a mounts the disk device. <n>
    <path> multi-mounts local partition n. -r remote-mounts another machine's
    9P export. -p/-c/-n bind the synthetic /proc, /dev/cons, and /net into the
    namespace.

SEE ALSO
    unmount, bind, cpu
